lowed_attempts": 2, "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}, {"type": "learning_skills", "contents": []}], "id": 11, "type": "RSLT"}], "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}]}], "stimuli": [{"_data": [], "contents": [{}], "template_override": 1, "id": 0, "type": "welcome"}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "contents": [{"value": {"coverimg": "enpe7n5le01ob10re2img01.jpg", "images": [{"time": "0", "text": "<span class=\"strong\"> Alice </span>: Hi, Tony. What have you been up to since the last time we met? <br>\n<span class=\"strong\"> Tony </span>: Alice, I have started a new job on data binding. <br>\n<span class=\"strong\"> Alice </span>: Interesting. I worked on that last year. We used the .NET framework to bind texts and other contents. <br>\n<span class=\"strong\"> Tony </span>: .NET Framework? I'm using traditional data binders. <br>", "image": "enpe7n5le01ob10re2img01.jpg", "id": 0}, {"time": "24000", "text": "<span class=\"strong\"> Alice </span>: Really? I'd rather you use .NET Framework to bind data. With .NET Framework you not only bind data, but also any structure of data; the way data appears on the source is not important. Let me give you some examples: with .NET you can set properties, such as the control for graphs and images, and the background color and size of the controls. <br>\n<span class=\"strong\"> Tony </span>: You're right. I'd rather work with .NET Framework from now on. What types of data binding are there? <br>", "image": "enpe7n5le01ob10re2img02.jpg", "id": 1}, {"time": "61000", "text": "<span class=\"strong\"> Alice </span>: There are two types of data binding: simple and complex data binding; I used simple data binding when I wanted to join a control to a single element from a data set. For example, a value in a column. If you are working with sets of data, you'd rather use the complex data binding, which consists in binding controls to more than one data element or even to different binding data types. Datagrid and Listbox are good examples of it. <br>\n<span class=\"strong\"> Tony </span>: Interesting, what are some common scenarios for data binding with .NET? <br>\n<span class=\"strong\"> Alice </span>: Almost every commercial application uses data binding to display information. Reporting requires lists and summaries that need to be displayed on the document. Data entry, which consists of data shown in boxes, is also a common scenario for data binding; master and detail apps, also use .NET to establish relationships between charts, and look up tables controlled by a combo box.", "image": "enpe7n5le01ob10re2img03.jpg", "id": 2}], "audiosrc": "enpe7n5le01ob10re2aud01"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "title": "", "id": 3, "type": "audio"}], "id": 0, "type": "scholar"}]}